      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Adding caffeine to Ritalin without a doctor's approval can increase your heart rate and cause jitters, which might worsen your anxiety during exams. Since your Ritalin isn't currently optimal for the intensity of your studying, the safest and most effective path is to consult your prescribing physician about adjusting your dosage or timing. They can provide a legal, tailored plan to help you manage your ADHD symptoms alongside your upcoming finals without risking side effects.",
